    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0476" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg402"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. van
                        Limburg</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 22d instant and of its enclosure, relative to the case of
                    the Netherlands ship Geziena Hildegonda, and to inform you that I have
                    transmitted a translation thereof to the Secretary of the Navy, whose attention
                    has been recalled to the matter.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, a renewed assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roest van Limburg.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
